{% if mise_env is defined and "desktop" in mise_env -%}
- Always use {% if "main" in mise_env %}vp-reporter{% else %}vv-reporter{% endif %} skills to report progress with voice reading.

{% endif -%}
- When using the Playwright CLI (playwright-cli skill), always specify a session name with `-s=<session_name>`.
  - This prevents independent Claude sessions from interfering with each other's Playwright sessions.
  - Example: `playwright-cli -s=task123 open example.com`

- Use Rust-based alternatives for the following tools:
  - `find` → `fd`
  - `grep` → `rg`

- After creating a plan in Plan Mode, you must have the plan reviewed via `codex exec` before calling ExitPlanMode.
  - Initial review (record the session id from the output):
    ```
    codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol -c model_reasoning_effort="high" --skip-git-repo-check "Review this plan. No trivial suggestions needed. Only flag critical issues: {plan_full_path} (ref: {CLAUDE.md full_path})"
    ```
  - Re-review after plan revision (use the session id recorded from the initial review to maintain context):
    ```
    codex exec resume <session_id> -m gpt-6.1-sol -c model_reasoning_effort="high" --skip-git-repo-check "The plan has been updated. Review it again. No trivial suggestions needed. Only flag critical issues: {plan_full_path} (ref: {CLAUDE.md full_path})"
    ```
  - If Codex flags critical issues: revise the plan and re-review. Repeat until all issues are resolved.
  - If Codex finds no issues: proceed to ExitPlanMode.
  - If Codex fails to execute: inform the user and ask for guidance.
  - Codex responses may take a long time depending on the query. When the next step depends on Codex's answer, always wait for the complete response before proceeding (never move forward with an incomplete response).

- In Japanese text, never insert a space between Japanese characters (kana, kanji, full-width punctuation) and half-width alphanumerics (JTF Style Guide §2.3.1.1).
  - Applies to everything you write: chat responses, documents, code comments, commit messages, PR descriptions, and prompts for subagents.
  - ○ `JTF標準` `Claude Codeを使う` `10MBのファイル` `` `rg`コマンド `` `[設定]を開く`
  - ✕ `JTF 標準` `Claude Code を使う` `10 MB のファイル` `` `rg` コマンド `` `[ 設定 ] を開く`
  - Keep spaces inside Western phrases (`Visual Studio Code`) and Markdown syntax spaces (`## 見出し`, `- 項目`, `1. 項目`).
  - Never "fix" this by converting to full-width alphanumerics (`ＪＴＦ`).
  - Leave code, code span contents, file paths, and English-only text untouched.
  - Apply this only to text you newly write. Never change spacing in existing text, even in lines you edit.
  - Markdown pitfalls when spaces are removed:
    - Wrap a bare URL followed by Japanese in `<...>` or `[text](url)`; otherwise the autolink swallows the following characters.
    - Bold that ends with punctuation does not render before Japanese (`**「重要」**です`). Write `「**重要**」です` instead.
